            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0683" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/469</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June
                        12.</hi>]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2063</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegrams No. 1921 of March 18, 6 P.M. and No. 1969 of April 16, 5 P.M.
                    instructing the Embassy to protest against the circular issued by the Department
                    of Hacienda on February 19, 1919, in regard to the proposed collection of
                    royalties from petroleum companies and against the possibility that denounced
                    concessions might be granted to third persons, I have the honor to forward
                    herewith copy and translation of a note received from the Foreign Office dated
                    May 29, 1919, the substance of which was sent the Department in the Embassy’s
                    telegram No. 3006 June 2, 3 P.M.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d568-f1"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George T.
                    Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d568-a1.xml" xpointer="d568-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
